window.ASHFALL_LOG = [{"ver":"0.8.0","title":"Blades, beams, auction house and the Ink league","groups":[{"title":"Melee: slashes and thrusts","items":["**Slashes**: reworked **Cleave**, **Cross Slash** (two crossing slashes), **Great Reaping** (205°, strong knockback). Area of effect enlarges the blow; multistrikes replay the swing, alternating direction, each blow a little wider.","**Thrusts**: a thin point that goes through — **Thrust**, **Impale** (+40% on the first enemy hit), **Flurry of Thrusts** (three points, uninterruptible), **Thunder Thrust** (arcs towards nearby enemies), **Frost Pike** (ice spikes bursting from the ground). **Gangrenous Strike** becomes a thrust.","**Shadows**: a new stat. Each shadow appears around the target and lands the same thrust at the same moment, for 70% of the damage (1 shadow on the opposite side, 2 in a triangle, etc.). Thrusts have no multistrikes.","Supports: **Twin Shadow**, **Pack of Shadows**, **Sharpened Shadows**, **Reach**, **Wide Sweep**, **Windmill**.","New **Master of Arms** talent tree (shadows, reach, multistrikes); **Master of Flow**: major talents reworked (Shadow Dance, Unbroken Flow, Great Spin).","Hero motions: animated thrusts and slashes, the hit timed to the swing and to attack speed. Dedicated sounds for every blow.","Weapons in hand: blade pointing down, grip in the centre of the fist; the hero's fingers are shorter."]},{"title":"Channelled beams","items":["**Ember Beam**, **Frost Beam**, **Lightning Beam**, **Void Beam**; reworked **Elemental Beam** (the element changes with stacks, Convergence at 55%).","The beam stops on the first enemy hit. **Refraction** (new stat): it splits from that enemy towards other targets, at half range; with no target, into mini-beams.","Area of effect widens the beam; **beam range** is a separate stat.","Supports: **Refraction**, **Lens**, **Wide Beam**, **Overload**, **Steady Flow**, **Mobile Beam**. **Prism of Knowledge** talent (Goddess of Knowledge).","Visuals fully remade: luminous energy specific to each element."]},{"title":"Auction house (characters in Trade mode)","items":["At creation, every character chooses **Trade** or **Solo (SSF)**. In Trade, an **Auction house** button appears in the right-hand menu.","**Buy**: Gear, Legendaries, Materials → slot (weapon type) → base → listings as large icons with their price; hover to compare with the item you wear. A home page with search and recently viewed entries.","**Line filters**: every possible line of the base, a min–max range filled from the chosen tier, nested **AND**, **OR** and **AT LEAST n** blocks.","**Sell** items and materials (unit or total price, 10% tax), **My sales** (Collect all), **History** with spending, income and taxes. An in-game notice tells you when something sells.","The market is simulated for now: fictional listings and buyers."]},{"title":"Ink league","items":["**Blank pages** of graph paper eat into some maps and release ink monsters; bringing colour back to the world fills vials.","The origami **Crane** settles at the refuge: with the vials, it opens the **Great Notebook**, a map made entirely of paper whose origami you free with a splash of ink.","**INK** branch of the Tree of the Lands, league cosmetics (trail, origami fox, portal), Ink title screen theme."]},{"title":"The game in English","items":["The whole game is translated: interface, skills, items, talents, dialogue, hints. The language is chosen in the options (menu or in game), with a suggested restart."]},{"title":"Game hints","items":["Hints now offer themselves discreetly on the left: **Guide me** starts the walkthrough, **Got it** closes it.","New hints: equipping an item, a new skill slot, your first aura, the forge, the loot filter. All of them can be read in the Codex and replayed (Options → Game).","Hints can be turned off per character. The movement controls are offered in game, after the introduction."]},{"title":"Characters and menus","items":["Every class starts with a level 1 **plain weapon**.","Hero or heroine, equipment visible on the character.","Character screen: weapon held on guard, Trade / SSF label, a bigger character; a cleaner creation screen.","Codex: **Bestiary** tab (defeated monsters, animated model, where to find each monster); Equipment tab with the icon and card of each item; right-click to move the camera.","Icons of every item base remade (bright stitched cloth, leather, metal, ash; one rank = one colour); four new belts. Skill and support icons are always framed."]},{"title":"Options","items":["Anti-aliasing as a single setting (FXAA, SMAA, TAA, MSAA 2x/4x/8x), **FSR 1 / FSR 2** upscaling, a **Details** setting.","Interface scale from 50 to 150%, and a separate **HUD scale**.","Controller: rebinding a button already in use frees the other action. More compact performance card (F3)."]},{"title":"Monsters","items":["New models: Wandering Dead, Pugnacious Goblin, Goblin Archer and Shaman, Bloodthirsty Ghoul, Vampire Noble, Blood Knight, Imp, Flame Summoner.","Runecarver: starts with the Ember Rune, Runic Carving at level 5."]},{"title":"Fixes","items":["Pets no longer jitter while following the hero.","Merchant: a real ember icon, a lighter window. Cleaner refuge chest and target frame."]}],"intro":"Two new melee families with their shadows, channelled beams, an auction house, the Ink league, the game in English and plenty of polish. Have fun!"},{"ver":"0.7.0","title":"The Runecarver, leagues and the Castle","groups":[{"title":"New class: the Runecarver","items":["**Runic Carving**: carves the runes of your 4 slots in turn (unlocked at levels 1, 6, 14 and 24, chosen in the Class tab). At most 4 glyphs at once.","Runes of **Embers** (fire), **Frost** (cold), **Thunder** (lightning) and **Withering** (erosion, formerly the Curse of Withering).","**Reactions**: two overlapping glyphs of different elements react — Thermal Fracture, Plasma, Superconduction, Black Flame, Frozen Necrosis, Void Arc.","**Word of Rupture**: detonates every glyph; all pairs react, with no cooldown.","**Resonance** (level 5): +40% reaction damage. A 12-node class tree (Catalysis, Cascade, Living Rune, Confluence…).","Engraved stones orbit the hero: the largest one is the next rune.","Rune supports: **Lasting Glyph**, **Unstable Glyph**, **Twin Rune**.","Legendaries: Chalk of the First Carver, Gauntlets of the Wandering Seal, Crown of the Four Seals, Ring of the Runic Round, Staff of the Great Cycle, Lexicon of Silence."]},{"title":"New skills","items":["**8 guards**, instant, without interrupting your action: Shield Overcharge, Unshakeable Guard, Mist Step, Stoneskin, Shield Wall, Aegis of Flames, of Frost and of the Storm.","**7 area curses** (one per enemy): Flames, Frost, Storm, Void, Torment, Fragility, Shattering. **Cursed Aura** support: the curse becomes an area around you.","**Empowerments** (8 s, +10% to skills of their type): **Martial Fervour** (+2% per nearby enemy), **Arcane Seal** (blood price: life lost, damage gained), **Creeping Blight** (a spore that Gnaws at enemies). **Convocation** becomes an empowerment: minions recalled to the cursor.","**Gangrenous Strike** (melee, stacking Gangrene)."]},{"title":"Plaguebearer and erosion","items":["Class rewritten around **erosion**: starts with **Contagion**, **Virulence** that rises with afflicted enemies, **Epidemic** at 100.","**Contagion**: a spore cloud that leaps to 2 enemies when its carrier dies (at most 4 leaps), with no loss of damage.","**Grasp**: a channel, erosion links on several enemies that leap on death.","**Scythe of Reaping**: **Reap** deals several seconds of all the target's damage over time at once.","**Poison is gone**: it becomes **hit erosion** (Serpent Fang; Venom renamed Corrosion for the Ranger).","Erosion spells deal real erosion hits, never reduced by elemental resistances. Black Hole switches to erosion.","Curse of Withering: 1 Wither per second unconditionally, erosion +75%.","Supports: Concentrated Virulence, Slow Agony, Reaper, Spread, Growing Rot, Withering.","Legendaries: Gauntlets of the Bloom, Gleaner's Ring, Crown of Rats, Plague Sower, Shroud of Eternal Rot, Scythe of the Last Hour."]},{"title":"Talents","items":["New god trees: **Lord of Minions** (all minions), **Master of Afflictions**, **Reaper of Plagues**, **Lord of Entropy**.","**Master of Legions** refocused on Bone minions, nodes renamed.","**Goddess of Knowledge**: new major talents (Refrain, Arcane Cycle, Inverted Hourglass, Anchored Runes, Wheel of Elements, Full Flow). A character who had the old choice keeps the new one of the same rank.","God choice reorganised into 5 paths, with a card for each tree.","Class tree: **right-click** to unlearn a node (if nothing depends on it)."]},{"title":"Skills: general pass","items":["Distances and areas finally shown correctly (the old calculation made them 1.7 times too short); some fifty descriptions corrected.","Tooltips: real damage per hit, ranges, rates, channelling cost per second, real minion life and damage, real aura values.","**Army of Bone**: one skeleton per cast, up to 4 (levels 1, 9, 17, 25), sturdier early on.","Elemental totems redesigned (pillars and gems), white-blue lightning everywhere, physical arrows in hot steel, a less blinding Frost Nova, a scorch of embers where the Fireball lands.","The totems' “Radiance” support renamed **Radiant Totem**.","Supports removed where they had no effect: Impulse without a cooldown, Crescendo on minions, Unstable Minions on Will-o'-wisps, Bounce on falling projectiles and the Lightning Orb…"]},{"title":"Space league","items":["**Invasions**: a black hole can open in the Wandering Lands (22%) and in the campaign from the 4th zone (20%). It spits out aliens from three families (Voracious Swarm, Crystallines, Void Abyssals) and implodes once the rift is emptied, dropping all the loot at once.","Closing an invasion yields **energy cells** (2 in the Wandering Lands, 1 in the campaign). The first one brings the **astronaut** to his island at the refuge.","**Expedition** (at the astronaut's): a crossing of asteroids, 1 cell per jump, up to a planet to conquer. Asteroids empower aliens and loot; encounters with choices (wreck, signal, anomaly, star shower).","**10 planets**, each with a permanent bonus that grows with its stars. **Solar system**: 3 orbits, alignments and family synergies.","**The Black Star**: 3 fragments open the map of the **Star Devourer** (three rifts then the Great Rift, 3 lives). Exclusive legendaries: Devourer's Crown, Event Horizon, Ring of the Dead Star.","Events on 10% of maps: meteor shower, supply drop, gravitational anomaly, golden alien.","New monsters: Voracious, Spine Spitter, Brood Crusher, Quartz Mite, Prismatic Mantis, Lumen Thrower, Void Crawler, Wandering Eye, Abyssal Maw; bosses the Brood Queen, the Quartz Tyrant, the Herald of the Void."]},{"title":"Glitch league","items":["**Glitched rifts**: 24% of Wandering Lands maps, 16% in the campaign from the 3rd zone. Enter with the interact key: the map “un-renders” itself and fills with bugs to fix.","4 types: **glitched**, **critical** (much stronger bugs), **volatile** (70 s), **recursive** (4 depths, then **the Corrupted Core**).","Bugs: Stray Byte, Stack Worm, Corruptor, Trojan Horse, Memory Leak.","**Glitched items**: one extra exclusive affix (Duplication, Null Pointer, Infinite Loop, Ghost Copy…). The forge cannot modify them.","Core legendaries, stronger with every glitched item you wear: Heart of the Core, Kernel Panic Mask, Null Pointer Blade.","The **Scientist** settles on the refuge's laboratory island: rift log, known affixes.","Tree of the Lands: 7 glitch nodes (Corrupted Packet, Recursion, Fatal Error…)."]},{"title":"Campaign and maps","items":["**New order**: act I (Forest Edge → Path of Bones → Catacombs → Marsh → Grounds), **act II = the Blood Castle** (Flooded Gaols, Great Halls, Apartments Wing, Nave of Blood, Rampart Walk, lv. 9–15), act VII = the desert (lv. 49–55). Old saves keep their finished maps.","**Brumevase Marsh** remade: walkways over the water, mist, fireflies, frogs, herons; the start at the foot of the burrow's mound; 108 monsters.","**Blood Castle Grounds** (new): an avenue, a fountain, a family cemetery, moats, a drawbridge, a breach into the gaols; rain, lightning, a blood moon that reddens as you approach. Guardian: the Crypt Beast.","**Rotating camera** in some zones (the Grounds), without ever changing the hero's direction; the minimap rotates with the camera (N marker).","Catacombs: torches with real flames, carved sarcophagi, translucent webs, more monsters; the exit through the mouth of the burrow onto a wooded meadow.","The Forest Edge: no more seaweed or tide pools, bark and driftwood remade, a lighter clearing around the hero (better performance).","Sound ambiences specific to each room of the Castle, to the Marsh and to the Grounds. Footsteps depend on the ground."]},{"title":"Guardians and monsters","items":["New Castle guardians: **The Headsman of the Gaols**, **The Scarlet Countess**, **Sir Morvan, Champion of Blood**, **The Guardian of the Nave**.","Castle monsters rebalanced; **the Blood Count** much faster and less tough.","**Grumm, the Gravedigger, the Lord of the Ossuaries**: richer models, entrances, a **second phase at 50%** with rage and new attacks.","Lord of the Ossuaries: a wide reap and a backhand, a spectral glide, −10% life.","Campaign guardian life less exponential (−10% at level 6, −43% at level 30). Zig-Zag, Great Goblin Oracle, less dangerous in the campaign."]},{"title":"Story","items":["**Rattles**, a chatty flying skull, follows you from the end of the Forest Edge to the refuge.","The Count's belongings reveal the flight of the ashen silhouette and a sea chart.","Voiced dialogue for the characters (Scientist, Astronaut, Merchant, Rattles…)."]},{"title":"Death and the Wandering Lands","items":["**Checkpoints**: you get back up at one third, two thirds or just before the guardian, as well as at the start of the map.","Death screen: **Get up**, **Restart** or **Return to the refuge** (the map stays open, RETURN portal).","Wandering Lands: **6 lives per map**.","Detailed death screen: the last 10 hits, their source and the calculation (armour, talents, shields)."]},{"title":"Refuge","items":["The refuge grows with you: camp, workshop, map pavilion, stone circle.","The astronaut's island and the laboratory island, linked by bridges once unlocked.","A more compact merchant."]},{"title":"Battle pass and cosmetics","items":["A free **battle pass** (J key): 61 challenges, 8 ranks from Recruit to Myth. Account-wide progress, challenges already met are counted as soon as it opens.","**Cosmetics** (pass points, no gameplay effect): 5 portals, 5 footstep trails, 5 pets (crab, frog, bat, swallow, will-o'-wisp), 4 title screen themes (Embers, Ashes, Cosmos, Glitch)."]},{"title":"Interface","items":["**Tutorial**: first talent, the Forest Edge chest (mana elixir), a support given by the first guardian, the class awakening. Can be turned off (Options → Game → Game hints).","A single interaction prompt at the bottom of the screen, with the real key.","New target and boss frames (affixes, ailments, ticks), a collapsible active effects bar.","Central announcements remade; simultaneous unlocks grouped together.","**F3**: performance card (hidden, compact, detailed).","Skill level-up: ▲ button, a panel above the key.","Loot filter in 3 screens, several named filters, a preview in a real clearing.","Character selection: class, progress, play time, drag-and-drop order. Key layout choice (ZQSD, WASD, mouse) at creation.","Sharper fonts at every resolution.","Steady loading, with no stall at 80%."]},{"title":"Options and controller","items":["Options → Display rewritten: window mode, screen choice, Low to Ultra presets, hover help; fullscreen at native resolution.","**Controller and Steam Deck**: assisted stick aiming, a virtual cursor in menus, A/R1… labels, settings adapted on first launch, help in Options → Controls."]},{"title":"Updates","items":["More reliable automatic updates: no more restart loop, file size and checksum verified, an `update.log` journal.","Downloads on a new server, with nothing to change on your side."]},{"title":"Fixes","items":["Shattering Leap: Trail of Fire, Momentum and Great Momentum work.","Shockwave: also works on Rush, Lunge, Shadow Leap and Whirlwind.","Elemental totems and Black Hole: the damage area matches the circle shown (85% before).","Burning Totem + Frenzied Totem: the burn ticks faster. Lightning Totem + Bounce: bounces count. Ice Totem: projectile speed applies.","Frost Arrow: shard speed counted only once. Sparks + All Around: spread over 360°.","Lightning Orb: text corrected (one discharge every 0.5 s). Rain of Arrows: displayed effectiveness is exact.","Spell Totem, Convocation and the Incendiary Arrow's trail placed at the real ground height.","Grasp: the damage arrives with the beam.","Ground effects (erosion, seals, fire) follow the terrain instead of being cut by slopes.","Catacombs: the hero no longer rises out of the ground at the start; candles and mushrooms without a floating base; the Lord of the Ossuaries' scythe the right way up; no more black pit at the exit.","Grounds: the dead hedges no longer float.","The Forest Edge: no more trees planted in the sand.","Refuge: foam around the pier posts re-centred, the boat's foam during the intro.","Rain follows the camera rotation; butterflies visible from above.","Death screen without the superfluous “Enter” hint; theme previews no longer stretched.","Sharp fullscreen: rendering followed the saved window size instead of the screen resolution."]}],"intro":"A ninth class, two leagues (space invasions and glitched rifts), the Blood Castle as act II, a battle pass, controller support and some thirty new skills. Have fun!"},{"ver":"0.6.5","title":"Living monsters, fearsome bosses and out into daylight","groups":[{"title":"Monsters","items":["**Animations fully remade** for the wolf, the crab, the goblins, the skeletons, the wandering dead and the spectres: feet that stay planted on the ground, real joints, distinct gaits depending on whether the creature wanders, hunts or attacks.","**Wolf**: real canine legs, a four-beat walk when it prowls, a **gallop** when it hunts; it crouches before leaping and bites while shaking its head.","**Crab** remade: a serrated shell, eyes on stalks, a big claw with a moving finger, and it **walks sideways**.","**Skeletons**: a stiff walk, a jerking head, dangling arms, a sword held for real; when they die, they collapse and **the skull rolls on the ground**.","**Wandering dead**: they limp, dragging a leg, arms reaching out to you.","**Ossuary Wraith** redrawn: it floats, its tattered robe ripples and trails behind it, a skull and glowing eyes under the hood, long claws; it is **translucent**."]},{"title":"Bosses","items":["**Grumm, King of the Trolls**: moss, mushrooms and a young tree on his back; he **tears out a boulder** to throw at you and makes **roots burst out** in three furrows.","**The Gravedigger**: candles and a raven on his coffin; **skeleton hands burst out under your feet**, the **souls of his lantern** hunt you down, and he flings earth with his shovel.","**The Lord of the Ossuaries**: bone wings and a soul flame; a **whirlwind of scythes**, a **cage of bone spikes** that closes around you and a **spiral of souls**.","Every attack is telegraphed on the ground before it strikes."]},{"title":"Morteval catacombs","items":["The bone walls follow the galleries, with no gaps at the corners; the staircases have their walls and are lit by braziers.","**New exit**: past the last door, an earthen tunnel climbs towards the light; you glimpse the surface as if leaving a burrow, then step out into a sunlit meadow."]},{"title":"Fixes","items":["The catacomb stairs are no longer black."]}],"intro":"The monsters of the first three levels finally move like real creatures, every boss has its own attacks and the catacombs lead out into the open. Have fun!"},{"ver":"0.6.4","title":"Cemetery, catacombs and a new forge","groups":[{"title":"Campaign","items":["**The Forest Edge remade**: a landing on a narrow beach, tidal woods, a living forest that closes in, a giant tree to walk around and a guardian at its feet. Butterflies, swallows, fireflies, grass that bends under your feet.","**Path of Bones (level 2) remade**: a dense forest, an edge of forgotten graves, the gate of the **Morteval cemetery**, rows of headstones, enclosures, a mourning angel, then a hill and a crypt. The light turns grey as you go.","**Morteval Catacombs (level 3), new**: a great staircase goes down beneath the crypt, then galleries lined with skulls and femurs, almost pitch black: your lantern cuts through the shadows, the candles flicker. At the end, the Lord of the Ossuaries.","New monsters: **cemetery skeletons**, **wandering dead**, **catacomb archers**, **ossuary wraiths**; bosses **the Gravedigger of Morteval** and **the Lord of the Ossuaries**.","Acts II and III: ten new campaign layouts (dunes, necropolis, canyon, flows, forges…), solid mineral scenery, no more end portals: you carry on along the path.","The Wandering Lands keep the original maps."]},{"title":"Progression","items":["**Campaign recompressed: level 1 at the start, level 55 on the very last map.** The Nightmares remain beyond.","World map: acts V to VII finally have their real layout (the climb of the Spire, the descent into the Depths, the approach to the Castle).","Slightly slower experience after level 20 (up to +25%).","**Wand damage now applies to spells**; no more imaginary bare-handed attack."]},{"title":"Forge","items":["The selection stays on the item after a confirmation.","**Auto-craft**: choose one or more target affixes with a minimum tier (e.g. “Strength T3 or better” or “Dexterity T2”), and the forge runs real attempts every half second, with the sound, the same chances and the same costs, until it succeeds or you run out of materials."]},{"title":"Interface","items":["**Loot filter remade**: rules on the left, an editor in the centre with grouped conditions, a real preview of the loot on the ground on the right; nine presets as cards; hidden loot can no longer be hovered or picked up (Alt shows it).","**Talent tree choice arranged in columns** (Physical · Melee, Magic · Elements, Shadow · Ranger, Defence · Support), without a scroll bar; the Back button works on the first choice.","Minimap: return and onward paths visible, locked in grey while the guardian lives."]},{"title":"Fixes","items":["**Terrain**: loot no longer falls under the ground on hills and stairs; Shattering Leap, rushes, ground spells and monster leaps and charges follow the terrain.","**Elixirs removed from the bar no longer come back** by themselves.","Solid scenery: no more walking through rocks and trunks, rushes included."]}],"intro":"The Verdeclat forest has been completely remade, a cemetery in the rain and bone catacombs await you, the forge can now craft on its own and the campaign goes up to level 55. Have fun!"},{"ver":"0.6.3","title":"Bestiaries and depths","groups":[{"title":"Monsters","items":["**A bestiary per act**, with no monster reused from one act to another: six monsters per act (melee, shooter, caster, leaper, brute, kamikaze) and two or three bosses, all remodelled and animated.","**Forest**: wolves, boars, goblins, goblin archers and shamans, moon-weaver spiders. Bosses: **Grumm, King of the Trolls**, the **Moon-Weaver Queen** and **Zig-Zag, Great Goblin Oracle**.","**Desert**: bone dogs, vultures, skeleton archers, **mummies**, bone colossi, sandstone golems. Bosses: the **King of Bones** and the **Necromancer of the Sands**.","**Rift**: imps, fire beetles, ash hounds, magma spitters, flame summoners, lava elementals. Bosses: **Ignar, Blazing Salamander** and **Morgrath, Lord of the Rift**.","**Coast**: crabs, shark sailors, buccaneers and three new pirates — the **Gunner**, the **Tide Witch** and the **Powder Monkey** (a barrel with a fuse). Bosses: **King Foam-Claw**, **Jaws** and **Captain Ashbeard**.","Bosses have more animations: ground slam, roar, spells, leap, summons.","Sizes harmonised: monsters are no longer tiny, bosses are about twice your size. Flying creatures stay in the air, and the life bar sits above each monster.","Eyes, runes, lava and crystals really glow."]},{"title":"Early access: acts V to VII","items":["**The Ashen Spire**: a mana sanctuary hanging over a chasm, six maps. Mana fires, crystal golems, spectral knights; bosses: the **Archon of the Reliquary** and the **Crystal Colossus**.","**The Sunken Depths**: reef, wreck, caves, dunes and trench, shafts of light, schools of fish, turtles. Fish-men, jellyfish, piranhas; bosses: the **Kraken of the Depths** and the **Siren Queen**.","**The Blood Castle**: halls, apartments, gaols, nave and ramparts. Vampire bats, gargoyles, blood knights; bosses: the **Blood Count** and the **Crypt Beast**."]},{"title":"Living scenery","items":["Forest: butterflies, swallows, fireflies, falling leaves, glowing mushrooms; trees and bushes in the wind.","Desert: layered sandstone walls, vultures, tumbleweeds, dust devils, nomad camps.","Rift: lava-veined basalt that pulses, embers and ash, geysers.","Coast and refuge: palm trees in the wind, gulls, butterflies."]},{"title":"Combat","items":["New **Mobile Casting** support: you can move while casting, at reduced speed (the penalty shrinks with level).","**Run while attacking**: the legs run while the upper body attacks or casts, the pelvis turns towards the direction of travel.","**Archery remade**: side-on, arm extended, string drawn to the cheek, arrow nocked, release. The arrow leaves when the string is released. Rain of Arrows fires in an arc. Between two shots, the stance is held, then the bow is lowered.","11 new supports: **Crescendo**, **Division**, **Far Shot**, **Deflagration**, **Charge Reserve**, **Economy**, **Mana Siphon**, **Spell Totem**, **Unstable Minions**, **Minion Guard**, **Penetration**."]},{"title":"Progression","items":["A steadier start: a little more experience is required in the first levels. Talents from level 2, class and passive at level 5, first ascension point at level 8.","**Tree of the Lands** opened at the first nightmare tier; its points come from nightmare maps completed for the first time. Acts not yet reached are locked on the map."]},{"title":"Fixes","items":["No more error when a monster that explodes on death dies just before the detonation.","Seamless black hole, refuge chest adjusted, padlocks drawn."]}],"intro":"Every act now has its own handmade monsters, the scenery comes alive and three new acts are open in early access. Archers finally shoot like archers. Have fun!"},{"ver":"0.6.2","title":"Bones, storms and a big clean-up","groups":[{"title":"Summoner and minions","items":["**Skeletal essence**: no more maximum number of skeletons; every Bone minion reserves essence (skeleton 30, archer 40, golem 70 out of a base 120). An essence gauge in the HUD.","New models for the **skeletons**, the **bone archers** and the **golem**; the enemy Bone Colossus wears armour.","Monsters **attack your minions**, who can die. Minions follow you from one zone to another, go around obstacles and no longer get stuck.","**Bone archers**: their arrows are real projectiles (pierce, bounce, return, all around, multiple projectiles…), fly further, glow, aim where the target is going, and the archer moves closer if its arrows cannot reach.","**Skeletons and golem** accept melee supports: **Multistrike**, **Shockwave**, **Quick Assault**.","New **Convocation** spell (instant): recalls all your minions to the cursor, +20% damage for 4 s.","New supports: **Legion**, **Brotherhood**, **Horde Frenzy**, **Multiple Summons**, **Elite**, **Prolongation**, **Fleetingness**, **Fast Projectiles**.","Three Bone legendaries: **Marrow of the Ossuary**, **Crown of the Lich King**, **Gravedigger's Seal**. Minion weapons (sceptres, totem staves) with their own affixes.","A single buff per minion skill, showing the number of living minions."]},{"title":"Talents","items":["**God trees reworked**: every rank adds the same value, strong effects have a single rank, two stats on a node have the same value, no more unrelated bonuses. Extra ranks are refunded automatically.","**Major talents** shown to the right of the tree: the three choices of each tier are readable at a glance, one click is enough.","Fixed: *Tactical Mastery* and *Grand Alchemist* **lengthened** cooldowns; the God of War's 7th column was open from 0 points.","Talent tooltips: small / medium / major talent, the current rank's effect line by line."]},{"title":"Supports and skills","items":["Support compatibility redone: a damage support no longer goes on a skill without damage, a cast speed support no longer on an instant spell.","**Instant** tag (elixirs, Convocation) compatible with **Preparation**; **Duration** tag: Prolongation and Fleetingness work on elixirs.","**Echo** (spells) and **Multistrike** (melee): beyond 100%, several repeats.","Renamed: Quick Assault, Quick Casting, Bounce."]},{"title":"World","items":["**Weather**: rain (from drizzle to downpour) and thunderstorms with lightning, at random on most maps and at the refuge — never in the lava rift.","**Night** can fall: a bluish moon, and a lantern lights your way.","**Desert** redesigned: less yellow light, less blinding spells, sandstone walls, and **five different layouts**.","**Refuge chest**: storage shared between all your characters, in front of the tent.","**Minimap**: a real map of walkable areas (galleon decks included), smooth outlines, a bluish discovery fringe, the boss pinned at the edge; the small map no longer shows items.","Boss music when the boss wakes."]},{"title":"Balance","items":["Experience curve and monsters reviewed (life, damage, act multipliers), a punchier early game.","Loot quantity depends on the nightmare tier; materials drop in **variable** amounts (no longer always 9 embers).","Forge unlocked at level 10. An equipped item placed on the anvil returns to its slot on confirmation."]},{"title":"Interface and comfort","items":["**Key bindings**: you can remove a skill from its key and bind it elsewhere, and two skills swap places correctly.","**Auto-equip** finally handles both rings.","Shields held correctly, axes the right way round.","Title screen background without facets; shadow and ambient occlusion options, MSAA 2x by default (better performance).","Target ailments that disappear with it, aura reservation aligned, lighter tooltips (active supports, archers).","Game icon on the EXE."]}],"intro":"The Summoner finally gets a real army, the world gains rain, storms and night, the talents are rebuilt and dozens of playtest reports are fixed. Thanks to all the testers!"},{"ver":"0.6.1","title":"Embers and sea spray","groups":[{"title":"Fire","items":["**Multiple ignites**: an enemy can burn several times at once (up to 4), each ignite dealing its own damage. Three ways to get more: the **Double Ignite** support, the **Pyre** class node and some legendaries.","New **Stoked Burn** support: +60% ignite damage for the linked skill.","**Spread**: hitting an already ignited enemy with a fire spell spreads the fire to its neighbour.","**Blaze** finally works: area fire spells leave a blaze on the ground that burns and ignites enemies.","**Contagious Heat**: a burning enemy can ignite its neighbour (no longer a duplicate of Wildfire).","**Overheat**: the gauge empties during the effect and then starts again from zero (before, a single spell was enough to restart it), and the bonus is shown with the other effects.","**Fireball** slower and with a shorter range. With **Return**, it explodes on impact or at the end of its flight, then comes back to you; if it hits an enemy on the way back, it explodes again. Pierce makes it go through.","**Deep Burn** weakened (+8% instead of +15%).","One word everywhere: you **ignite** an enemy."]},{"title":"Spells and skills","items":["**Chain your spells**: every skill waits for its own cast time, but you can cast another spell, teleport or drink an elixir in the meantime. No more Meteor blocking your Blink!","**Swift Archer** no longer applies to spells; new **Swift Sorcerer** support (+30% cast speed for projectile spells).","**Meteor**: the warning area exactly matches the area hit, and the burning ground is clearly visible, including in boss arenas.","Brand new **burning ground** (Meteor, Blaze, Trail of Fire); several overlapping areas do not deal more damage.","**Sprint** elixir: +30% speed (instead of 45%). **Rage** elixir: no more movement speed. **Potent Brew**: +20% effect, without changing the duration."]},{"title":"Talents","items":["Every node gives **one strong effect and one small one**, no more four-line nodes.","No more four-node paths: **paths of two or three nodes**, more of them, with 34 new nodes across the eleven god trees."]},{"title":"Music and ambience","items":["**Real composed music**: a theme per act, plus the refuge, the arena and the bosses. In zones, the music gives way to quiet moments.","**Recorded ambiences**: birds in the forest, desert wind, the rumble of the volcano, waves and gulls on the coast and at the refuge.","Music and ambience change correctly from one map to another (act I no longer plays the beach)."]},{"title":"Interface","items":["A compact target frame, with ailments shown below; it no longer flickers.","An **energy shield** bar in a clear blue, with no stray line when it is full.","Clicking a skill or support slot puts the cursor straight into the search.","No more “Support unlocked” message when opening a slot with energy.","The character sheet shows the chance to ignite, ignite damage and the number of simultaneous ignites."]}],"intro":"Fire rethought from top to bottom, real music and recorded ambiences, spells that finally chain freely. Have fun!"},{"ver":"0.6.0","title":"The Wreckers' Coast","groups":[{"title":"Act IV: the Wreckers' Coast","items":["**Five new zones** (levels 45 to 57): beaches, fords to wade across, lagoons, rocks and the wreck of a **stranded galleon** you explore from bow to stern.","The terrain finally has **height**: you climb dunes, wade knee-deep into the water, cross walkways.","**New enemies**: shark sailors, reef crabs, buccaneers… and fins circling the fords.","**Three new bosses**: King Foam-Claw, Jaws the boatswain and the fearsome **Captain Ashbeard**."]},{"title":"The island of Hautecrête","items":["The refuge becomes a **real tropical island**: a living sea with waves and foam, wet sand, footprints, a crackling campfire, palm trees, rocking boats and a pier to stroll along.","The **training dummy** has its own islet, linked by a bridge."]},{"title":"Nightmares and campaign","items":["**Four Nightmare tiers** instead of ten, but longer: each tier replays the whole campaign and the zone level rises from one act to the next (Nightmare I: levels 58 to 73… up to level 100).","Acts unlock **in order**: no jumping straight to act III with a new character."]},{"title":"Strength, Dexterity and Intelligence","items":["Three new **attributes**: each point grants **+0.5% damage** to the skills that carry that attribute (Strength for Cleave, Intelligence for Fireball, Strength and Dexterity for Whirlwind…).","They appear on items, in the talent trees and on the character sheet; each skill's tooltip shows its attributes and the current bonus.","**Five new legendaries** built around attributes: Wrestler's Belt, Scholar's Crown, Fox Stride, Titan's Grip and Ring of the Three Ways."]},{"title":"God trees","items":["Small nodes give **generic damage**: a tree stays useful after an element conversion.","Nodes that **reduce mana cost** now come at the start of every tree.","**Some thirty new effects** for end nodes and major talents, always mixing attack and defence: *War Cry*, *Riposte*, *Ambush*, *Colossus*, *Back to the Wall*, *Transfusion*, *Close Guard*…","**Guardian of the Bastion**: your armour and your blocks become damage. **Alchemist**: less focused on elixirs, your regeneration feeds your blows.","Major talents show their icon once chosen."]},{"title":"Legendaries and items","items":["Legendaries act on **whole families**: Phoenix Heart sets all your fire damage ablaze, Twin Dawn makes any melee attack strike twice…","Legendaries that had no effect of their own received one.","More **Special** and **Ultimate** affixes to forge, including a new rare ultimate that **reduces aura reservation** (helmet and chest).","Clearly visible rarity frames in the inventory and equipment: you spot a legendary at a glance."]},{"title":"Characters","items":["**Faces fixed** (they took on the class colour) and **outfits in each class's colours**.","New **staves, wands and sceptres** for spellcasters.","An **emblem** for each class and an icon for each passive.","**Dedicated icons** for every talent, ascendancy and active effect (no more empty boxes in the effects bar)."]},{"title":"Title screen and selection","items":["A **new animated title screen**, with two moods to choose from: **Embers** or **Ashes**. Loading screens follow the chosen theme.","Entrance animations, a transition to character selection and a glowing pedestal in your class colours.","The character card shows your progress (“Act 2 · Nightmare I”) and your passive, also during creation.","The **patch notes** can be read straight from the title screen."]},{"title":"Interface","items":["A **new font**, sharp at every resolution.","Elixirs show their **charges** on the skill bar, like a cooldown.","A wider forge: no more cut-off text in the possible results.","Tabs that no longer jump on hover, lighter tooltips, the Forge button highlighted.","In fullscreen, the chosen resolution applies to the game's rendering."]},{"title":"Balance","items":["An aura that would reserve more than 100% of your mana switches off instead of leaving you dry.","**Whirlwind**: lower starting speed, but every channelling spin increases speed and area.","**Crush** stuns less often; **Fortification** and **Fragility** work as advertised.","Fighting **bare-handed** early in the game is no longer a punishment.","Elixirs unlock for your character as soon as you find them; drinking again resets their duration."]},{"title":"Fixes","items":["The class tree could show **8/7 points** and lock a point: fixed.","Some temporary talent bonuses never ended.","The Plaguebearer had lost its appearance.","The target bar no longer flickers and the life bar no longer causes an error on death."]}],"intro":"A fourth act by the sea, an island remade from top to bottom, rethought talent trees and a brand new title screen. Safe crossing!"},{"ver":"0.5.0","title":"The ash forge","groups":[{"title":"Forge","items":["Forge remade from top to bottom: three affix qualities — **Normal**, **Special** and **Ultimate** — each with its own stats. A line no longer shows “maximum life” in all three qualities: each quality brings different, increasingly powerful effects.","**Before/after comparison** right in the panel: the old and the new version of the item side by side, an arrow between them, the changed line highlighted in red (before) and green (after). No more separate window.","**Cancel / Reforge / Confirm** buttons under the comparison; the right-hand panel always keeps the materials and possible results.","**Caps**: two special and two ultimate affixes per item, prefixes and suffixes combined. Lines that are already special or ultimate shine in their colour, and the pool stays viewable even when the cap is reached.","**Protected T1**: reforging a line already at the best tier asks for confirmation, with a “Don't ask again this session” box.","**T1 tier**: a golden halo on the item card and a satisfying sound; no more stray text or confetti.","High-level items: the worst tiers are removed from the roll (always at least three tiers), and the best tier becomes the rarest — about 17% T1, 33% T2, 50% T3.","Tiers shown **to the left** of the lines in a stylised frame, with a gradient colour (gold → pink → turquoise → blue → purple) identical in every window.","Rerolls, re-energising and corruption moved to the centre, under the affixes: they apply directly, only the forge goes through the comparison.","Belt affixes finally talk about **elixirs** rather than potions."]},{"title":"Characters and balance","items":["A **single basic skill** per class: the others are earned in play.","Start without equipment, without an aura or an elixir.","Flat level bonus removed from attacks and fixed-damage weapons: no more damage exploding without gear.","Cast and attack speed shown in attacks/second, with the time per cast.","Reliable auto-equip (both rings in the same click) and a DPS/toughness comparison in the tooltip."]},{"title":"Interface and comfort","items":["Generated icons for items, materials, skills, classes and talents, **sharp at every interface scale**.","**Clicking an equipped item**: a pinned tooltip, hoverable keywords and a direct **Forge** button.","Item tooltip: energy as a bar, fixed damage, required level highlighted.","Unlock banners with the icon of the skill or support.","Sharper interface fonts, lighter comparison and forge texts."]},{"title":"Options and display","items":["**Window resolution**: 720p, 900p, 1080p, **2K** and 4K (window re-centred; ignored in fullscreen).","**Interface scale** from 75% to 200% on a continuous slider.","Five volumes (master, effects, interface, music, ambience) applied live, showing **Mute** at zero; the music resumes as soon as you raise its slider.","Icons follow the screen's real resolution, with no blurry upscaling."]},{"title":"Audio and world","items":["Generated music and ambiences for every act, zone and boss; interface, forge and unlock sounds reworked.","Hub on the island of Hautecrête, acts II and III, Quaternius and Kenney scenery, floors without visible tiles."]},{"title":"Fixes","items":["Missing music when launching from the menu, volume sliders with no effect, failing class start tests.","Tooltips that stayed stuck, item comparison and inventory sorting."]}]},{"ver":"0.4.0","title":"Three acts, fifteen dungeons","groups":[{"title":"World","items":["A campaign in three acts and fifteen dungeons: the Verdeclat forest (a1–a5), the Desert of Bones (a6–a10), the Scarlet Rift (a11–a15), each with its own theme, palette and music.","The hub becomes an island resting on the sea: painted sand, a sloping beach, foam on the shore and an animated swell; scenery reduced to the dummy and the war table.","Cleaned-up scenery: only the Kenney and Quaternius kits are used, white materials fixed, basalt walls in the rift, a cart and beach props."]},{"title":"Combat and readability","items":["Attack telegraphs per enemy type: arcs, circles and lines on the ground, coloured by element — you see the blows coming.","An endless arena with waves, elites and best wave tracking.","Nightmare modifiers rolled when each map opens (16 affixes, three per tier)."]},{"title":"Items and interface","items":["Loot filter by rarity, automatic comparison with the equipped item, DPS and toughness auto-equip button.","Abbreviated damage numbers (k), a scrolling character list, a second skill on right-click."]},{"title":"Class variants","items":["Every class now has its own palette: cloth, hair and the glow of the eyes change, the silhouette reads at a glance in a crowded arena."]},{"title":"Audio","items":["Five buses (master, effects, music, interface, ambience) with sliders that really apply, even when the game is paused.","Music and ambience for every act, zone and boss; the act I theme re-recorded."]},{"title":"Rendering","items":["No more visible tiles on the ground: textures re-centred on their detail, decorrelated ground noise and shadows in a single cascade.","The hub's water fully repainted (swell texture, foam in two strokes, translucent fringe) and an invisible wall before the slope."]}]},{"ver":"0.3.0","title":"Lands, legendaries and a visual overhaul","groups":[{"title":"World and characters","items":["Eight playable classes: Ember Guardian, Arcanist, Ranger, Summoner, Pyromancer, Frostweaver, Stormcaller and Plaguebearer, with their mechanics and class trees.","Animated Quaternius characters for the eight classes, the Imp and the Pugnacious Goblin; lighter character models and weapons correctly attached to the hands.","Quaternius nature, village and craft scenery in the castle and the zones; first Quaternius sword, axe and shield looks.","A longer campaign, ten nightmare tiers and progressive zone levels. Tree of the Lands, chests and map bonuses.","Pre-computed levels and resource preloading to reduce hitches. Fixed duplicated models and leaks when loading pre-computed scenes."]},{"title":"Combat and progression","items":["Elemental Beam remade: a persistent beam that follows the cursor without leaving old traces, distinct ice, fire and lightning effects, glyphs at the ends. A new Beam tag and a fix for damage bonuses per stack.","All Around and Return supports; fixes to totem projectiles, their limit and Deployment. Incompatible supports removed from Rain of Arrows.","Multiple hits: the first projectile of a cast deals full damage, the following ones 70% on the same target.","Energy on items of level 40 and above for supports; costs, compatibilities and weapon restrictions detailed.","Talent exclusivities removed. A new three-rank node in the Fire, Frost and Lightning trees: physical to element conversion, up to 100%. Fair stacking with supports.","Descriptions corrected, notably Barrage. Central notifications queued for unlocked skills, supports and slots, including when several levels are gained at once."]},{"title":"Items and forge","items":["Thirty more legendaries: 48 in total, with four rarity tiers, from the common T4 to the extremely rare T1.","T4 legendaries reworked to offer real levelling alternatives to rares, with specialities and trade-offs.","Several legendaries' identities strengthened; tiers visible on new items as well as old ones. Fixed negative modifiers at generation.","Choice of the main skill for damage comparisons, implicit energy and re-energising at the forge."]},{"title":"Interface and comfort","items":["A new main menu and character selection: previews loaded in the background, caching and class changes without rebuilding the screen.","Character switching removed in game: selection and creation only from the main menu.","A single real loading screen from the moment the character launches, with no intermediate screen.","A Codex of hoverable keywords and tooltips, available from the pause menu.","Options: frame limit from 30 to 360 with a slider, keyboard input and an unlimited mode; anti-aliasing, 3D resolution, bloom, loot visibility, buffs and life bars.","DEV tools: all Torments, +50 Tree of the Lands points and a catalogue of the 48 legendaries sorted by tier and slot, with direct generation of the chosen item.","Fixed the account reset and strengthened test isolation to protect player saves."]}]},{"ver":"0.2.0","title":"Channelling, forge and comfort","groups":[{"title":"What's new","items":["Summoner class (minions, Legion / Bone / Spirits tree, Bone Golem).","Stacking channelling: every channelled skill builds a buff (Whirlwind: +10% area per stack). New “max stacks” and “starting stacks” stats (Tornadoes and Nascent Vortex talents).","Whirlwind remade: clean rotation, new visual effect, slow from −20% (lv. 1) to −10% (lv. 20).","Any skill interrupts a channel. New Dance Step support: the movement skill does not interrupt it (Whirlwind + Blink).","Multistrike really repeats the attack; a new multistrike chance stat (beyond 100%, up to 3 strikes).","Rush knocks down and briefly stuns; Lunge remains a small leap (no more crossing the map with attack speed).","Training dummy: START / STOP button in its panel, untouchable until it is started.","A bigger hub (fountain square, forge, training, war table, market)."]},{"title":"Forge and items","items":["Selected modifier framed, possible results with the range of the highest reachable tier, a sound and a flash with every forge.","Strictly increasing affix tiers (a tier's minimum always exceeds the lower tier's maximum).","Embers and crystals much rarer."]},{"title":"Balance","items":["Experience: half as much XP per level. Auras unlocked at levels 15, 25, 35 and 50.","Base life and mana regeneration reduced (the value shown is the real value).","Ground trails no longer stack on the same monster and are much cheaper.","Mind Over Matter works (50% of mana as energy shield)."]},{"title":"Interface","items":["Hover effects on clickable elements, major talents viewable even when locked.","Options: hide magic items on the ground, monster (red) and ally (green) life bars can be toggled.","The icon of the skill used for the estimated DPS, elixirs back in the skills, stable slots when changing key bindings.","Automatic channelling: the character follows the cursor, a new click stops it; no more sliding during attacks."]}]},{"ver":"0.1.0","title":"First playable version","groups":[{"title":"Content","items":["A 5-level campaign in the Verdeclat Forest, winding layouts with no dead ends, a boss at the end of each level.","Global nightmare level: finish the whole campaign to unlock the next tier (+16 monster levels).","Endless arena: endless waves, choice of starting wave, personal record.","3 classes (Ember Guardian, Arcanist, Ranger) with a class passive and a branching ascension tree.","11 talent trees (War, Knowledge, Hunt, Flames, Frost, Lightning, Afflictions, Bastion, Mana, Alchemy, Legions) with major talents at tiers 10 and 20.","Skills, supports and auras to unlock for the whole account, gems up to level 20.","Movement skills (Rush, Blink, Shadow Leap, Lunge) and damage over time skills (Toxic Cloud, Curse of Withering, Burning Totem).","Elixirs with charges earned by killing monsters, unlocked after the first map.","Bows, two-handed weapons, off-hand (dual wielding or shield), legendaries for every slot."]},{"title":"Combat","items":["Armour, evasion, block, resistances (max 60%, can be raised) and energy shield with a recharge delay and speed.","Skill slots unlocked over the levels, auras from level 20."]},{"title":"Forge","items":["Normal, special and ultimate modifiers (ultimates from ilvl 40), tiers limited by item level.","One-click reforging, rerolling one line or the whole item, corruption."]},{"title":"Interface","items":["“Geometric Forge” interface, vector icons in 5 styles to choose from.","Detailed tooltips for skills (current and next level) and items.","Options: sound, display, game, controls, what's new.","Automatic update at startup."]}]}];
